WEBVTT

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.800
Dr. Bashir, the time is 0500.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.280
Yeah, all right.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:16.940
We have to get up.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:20.670
Big day.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.090
It's a big night.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:29.820
Clear that block.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:41.000
of unanswered questions such as such as just how far these spots really go down I suppose you

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:54.990
want to tell miles do that because you tell him everything you know I'm gonna make an exception

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:01.770
We really should get up.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.950
We don't want the Defiant leaving without us.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.480
You know, I've never been into battle with someone I've slept with before.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.060
Oh, there's a first time for everything.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.350
Now that we're finally together, it'd be such a shame if something happened to one of us.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:20.900
Let's make a pact.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:22.940
We both come home alive.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:24.990
You got yourself a deal.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.260
I'm holding you to that.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.880
Oh, and don't forget, Kiryoshi has his check up at 0900 tomorrow.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.060
I've already confirmed the appointment with Nurse Bandy.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.220
Come on, sweetie, one more bite.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.400
And don't stay up all night writing that paper on...

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.340
What are those trees called?

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.160
Our filian ficus, and they're not trees, they're shrubs.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.380
Yeah, well, try to get some sleep.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:52.250
Oh, and...

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.530
Honey, we'll be fine. Stop worrying.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.970
All right. Molly, please don't touch...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.600
I let you play with my toys.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.020
Yeah, but see, this isn't a toy.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:07.110
This is a model.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:09.230
Maybe it belongs in a museum, then.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:15.230
I suppose I could give it to Julian.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:16.980
Sounds good to me.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:21.210
Speaking of Julian, have you told him about Starfleet's offer yet?

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.540
Uh, no, not yet.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.000
What's that supposed to mean?

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.630
We're not going back to Earth.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:29.960
Of course we are.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.170
Daddy's going to teach at the academy when the war's over.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.490
You haven't even told Julian.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:39.490
Out of the mouth of babes.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.800
I'll tell him, you know, when I think he's ready to hear it.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:52.930
Oh, it still wanders from my head, but it's my stomach that's bothering me.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.330
If it will help, morning sickness ends after the first trimester.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.970
Oh, that's two more months. I don't think I'm going to...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:07.850
Ben, promise me something.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.300
Promise that you'll come home to us.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:18.040
I don't believe it.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.360
I said I promise.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.640
No, it's not.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:25.700
Hey.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.740
I thought I'd walk you to the Defiant.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.480
I like that.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.570
How's Cass?

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:45.880
Reports of my death have been exaggerated, but not by much.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.430
Isn't there something she can take to make her feel better?

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:54.940
She doesn't like taking medication unless it's absolutely necessary.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:57.110
Sounds necessary to me.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.980
Waiting for you to leave only makes me feel...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.250
worse. If you're gonna go, just go.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:08.280
Sure, I can't get

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:19.600
you anything. Mind if I walk with

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.230
you, Commander? Not at all. Captain

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.230
Sisko informed me that you would be joining us on

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:27.560
the mission. I hope that when we reach Cardassia

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.240
we find Colonel Kira alive

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:29.660
and well.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.610
So do I, Commander. So do I.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.080
Captain on the bridge!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.100
Alright, people. What do you say we end this war?

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:46.610
Sounds good to me.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.490
Ensign, I believe you know the way to Cardassia.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:52.270
If I get lost, I'll just follow the ship in front of us.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:03.740
The Federation invasion fleet has left Deep Space Nine.

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:07.540
They'll reach the Cardassian border by tomorrow night.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:12.560
Our brave Jem'Hadar soldiers have a motto.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:14.980
Victory is life.

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:19.620
I'm glad you're familiar with it.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:23.060
Because today those words have meaning for us all.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.980
The outcome of this battle will determine the outcome of the war.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.970
Either we destroy their invasion...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:39.880
forces or they destroy us there is no other option fight well today and Romulus will be

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:54.630
yours to do with as you wish yes yes and earth too I assure you the pleasure is all mine

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.150
Is something bothering you?

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:17.970
Apparently, I was under the mistaken impression that all Federation territories would fall under my jurisdiction, including Earth.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.060
And so they shall.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:25.100
But promise the Breen.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:29.960
I would promise the Breen the entire Alpha Quadrant, if I thought it...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.380
I would help win this war.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:38.050
Founder is wise in all things.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:47.360
Founder, I've heard a disturbing rumor about the traitor Damar.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:48.480
What about him?

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:50.640
He may be alive.

00:08:51.770 --> 00:08:52.790
Is this possible?

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.460
I don't see how. We destroyed his ship, his rebel bases.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.200
But his body was never found.

00:08:58.520 --> 00:08:59.880
They say he's here.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.560
On Cardassia Prime, in the capital no less.

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:05.090
Look into this matter.

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:11.280
If Tamar is alive, he won't be for long.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:30.720
Halt!

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:32.410
Step forward.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:33.710
Slowly.

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:35.090
I'm sorry.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.010
Have we done something wrong?

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:38.530
We're new to this city, and I'm afraid we're lost.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:38.850
Quiet!

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:42.260
You are Liggett Damar.

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:44.510
I told you, you look just like him.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:47.670
I can't tell you how many times my cousin has been mistaken for that traitor.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.590
He will be taken to Dominion headquarters.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:52.100
You will die here.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.060
I do not understand you.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:08.140
Hey, don't mean to sound ungrateful, but what are you doing here?

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:09.630
Watching your backs?

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:12.910
I thought we decided it would be safer if you stayed out of sight.

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:15.750
Helmets for you. You should be wearing one, too.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:19.550
Every Jem'Hadar and Breen soldier on Cardassia is looking for you.

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:22.330
If I'm to lead this revolt, I can't do it hiding in a cellar.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:24.840
It was necessary for me to attend that gathering tonight.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:29.890
Well, fill me in later. If anyone stops us, you're my prisoner.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:37.580
But the vote was unanimous. The work disruptions begin tomorrow.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:42.060
Power, communication, and transportation facilities throughout Cardassia will be sabotaged.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:44.820
The Dominion fleet will be cut off from all ground support.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.280
That way they'll have to face the invasion force on their own.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.860
Once the Dominion is crushed, all Cardassia will be free again.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:55.240
Oh, when you were a small boy, I was worried about you.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:58.220
Always getting into trouble.

00:10:58.830 --> 00:10:59.970
So secret.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.080
so full of deceit.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.910
Who would have thought those disgraceful characteristics

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:08.230
would be turned to virtues?

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:11.050
Morty?

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:12.330
You're too kind.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:24.650
You're the chief?

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:29.300
Sounds like the Doppler compensators are out of phase.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:31.760
Ensign, how's she handle it?

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.240
She's not quite as smooth as the old Defiant, sir.

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:36.160
Feels a bit sluggish.

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:37.340
Chief?

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:38.220
Come on it.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:39.560
I'll grind to engineering.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:40.560
Engineering.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.730
Recalibrate the inertial dampers.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:45.070
Check the plasma flow regulators while you're at it.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:45.980
Right away, Chief.

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:49.050
I think someone would have come up with a better inertial control system.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:49.870
Was that Miles?

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.330
I said I wish you'd wipe that grin off your face.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.680
You're not the first person to fall in love, you know?

00:11:58.920 --> 00:11:59.980
I thought you'd be happy for...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:08.050
me i am happy for you who brought to engineering engineering now try realigning the induction coils

00:12:08.050 --> 00:12:17.560
will do you're sure you're not angry why should i be angry i have been asking you to tell the

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:24.280
doctor how you feel about him for the past month well now that he knows how i feel i am happy for

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:29.000
you that's a relief but am

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:41.960
going to kill him you're kidding right and jadzia said i did not have a sense of humor julian

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:47.380
there's something i need to talk to you about you're getting pressure from keiko on you how did

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:53.430
you know that's a big decision i'm surprised didn't come up sooner actually we've been

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:58.050
talking about it for quite a while well you can stop talking about him we'll move the alamo into

00:12:58.050 --> 00:12:59.970
my quarters i could still

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:06.200
use a little more equalization on the torque buffers. Right. I'll try to compensate with

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:10.120
the impulse response filters. That way your quarters won't be so cluttered, and you can

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:16.530
still use it whenever you want. I wasn't talking about the Alamo model. Besides, it's

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:21.780
too big for your quarters. You let me worry about that. So, what were you talking about?

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:29.630
Oh, it's nothing that can't wait. Is that any better, Nug? Torque buffers are stable.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:31.860
I wish you were here too, Constable.

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:38.800
If we all knew where Kira was,

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.680
if we could only be sure that she was all right.

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.130
Colonel's a survivor.

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:51.000
This war, Captain, it has to end.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:55.560
And it will, soon, one way or the other.

00:13:57.590 --> 00:13:59.980
Mother, the emissary...

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:09.080
task is nearing completion are you talking about the war you have walked the path the prophets laid

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:27.720
out for you benjamin do not falter now i don't intend to know this my son your journey's end lies

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:28.780
It's not before you.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:31.840
But behind you.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.280
Captain, Captain.

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:43.650
Marvitz came to me in a vision.

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.700
I take it they weren't bringing good news.

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:51.080
I'm not sure.

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:54.040
The time will tell.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.320
Hello, Adami.

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:09.960
You're back.

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:16.370
All you have to say to me.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.530
I see the Power Wraiths have restored your sight.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:23.900
Yes, they've forgiven me.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:28.160
I was hoping you could find it in your heart to do the same.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:29.980
I don't forgive.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:40.030
of war criminals. To think I took Dukat to my bed, one of the most hated men in Majoran

00:15:40.030 --> 00:15:47.280
history. I've already told you how much I regret my actions during the occupation. Of course

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:59.840
you do. Have you learned how to release the parades? The secrets of the coast, Amogen.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.220
have been revealed to me, yes.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:05.310
Then why haven't you gone to the fire caves

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:06.210
and freed them?

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:08.370
I was waiting for you.

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:18.200
I need your help, Dukat.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:19.440
It's as simple as that.

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:23.660
All I have to do is ask.

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.840
Together we will release the Palwraiths

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:29.890
so they can lay claim to the celestial temple.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.860
and destroy the pits.

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:34.260
And their emissary.

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:42.360
Benjamin Sisko will be dealt with by me and me alone.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:46.110
Assuming he survives the invasion of Cardassia.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:49.990
Oh, he'll survive, but I promise you,

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:53.420
he'll wish he hadn't.

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:12.580
Got any threes?

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:21.140
You can tell me you're quitting.

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:22.760
It's just not my game.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:24.660
What, you want to try a pinochle again?

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:26.280
How about rummy?

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:27.340
Or gin rummy?

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:28.890
Five cards to that?

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.500
Canasta.

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:32.100
How about some Tongo?

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:34.940
Did they play Tongo in Las Vegas in 1962?

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.930
How could they? It's a Ferengi game.

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:40.500
Which is why my holographic program can't create it.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:43.200
I know, I know. This place is period-specific.

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:48.960
For a hologram, not very accommodating.

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:51.580
Oh, is that why you dropped by to insult me?

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:54.620
I dropped by because I had nothing else to do.

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:57.580
My bar hasn't had half a dozen customers all day.

00:17:59.020 --> 00:17:59.980
Everyone's off fighting their...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:07.240
stupid war. It's not easy staying behind, is it? Knowing your friends are out there

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:13.830
risking their lives. They think they have it rough? They should try leading my life

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:19.610
for a day. The hospitality industry isn't for the faint-hearted. A bartender's life

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:26.440
is a lonely one. That's true. Few people understand it. They think it's one big happy party. They

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:29.860
forget that the person giving the party never has any fun. He's too busy making

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:36.580
sure everyone else is having fun. All I do all day long is give, give, give.

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:42.030
Bartending is a very noble profession, and you do it well. Under some very

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:44.430
difficult circumstances, I might add. You should be proud.

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:46.640
Think so?

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:48.300
I know so, Pally.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:56.420
I just hope Nog and the rest of those heroic idiots come back in one piece.

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:57.560
There you are.

00:18:58.850 --> 00:18:59.970
Vic, sweetie, are you...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.340
Are you ready? Jimmy and Peter are about to go on.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:05.320
Sorry pal, you gotta run.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.470
Durandy and Lawford are at the Sands.

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:08.890
Can't miss that.

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:12.700
I thought you said a bartender's life was a lonely one.

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:15.400
It is, but I'm not a bartender.

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:27.210
Go fish.

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:48.080
Is it really necessary to rest so often?

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:52.180
You need to wait for me.

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:53.040
Go on ahead.

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:58.230
Wander aimlessly through these caves for the rest of your miserable life.

00:20:01.596 --> 00:20:02.716
I'm in no hurry.

00:20:06.044 --> 00:20:08.044
During the occupation,

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:12.780
My people found the Bajoran's fear of these caves.

00:20:13.468 --> 00:20:14.028
Amusing.

00:20:15.548 --> 00:20:18.288
And yet we never took the time to visit them.

00:20:19.964 --> 00:20:21.104
And now here I am.

00:20:23.036 --> 00:20:24.176
It's ironic, isn't it?

00:20:25.148 --> 00:20:25.988
I don't care.

00:20:28.316 --> 00:20:29.996
Excuse me, I just

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.900
I'm sure you have many interesting anecdotes about the occupation.

00:20:34.796 --> 00:20:36.896
But I don't have any desire to hear them.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.700
I meant no disrespect, Adami.

00:20:40.108 --> 00:20:40.668
And stop.

00:20:40.748 --> 00:20:41.788
Calling me a dummy.

00:20:43.116 --> 00:20:44.996
That privilege is no longer yours.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.520
How should I address you then?

00:20:50.252 --> 00:20:53.152
From now on, you will address me as eminence.

00:20:53.708 --> 00:20:54.408
Is that clear?

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:58.940
perfectly

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:19.330
Eminence I see your point, but for two millennia the Jem'Hadar have been the Dominion's first line of defense

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:24.190
It will damage their morale to have to take a back seat to the Breen

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:29.820
Very well in the spirit of our new alliance

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:35.420
I will inform the Jem'Hadar that the Breen forces will stand alongside them.

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:39.210
I'm glad that pleases you.

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:41.010
I think we have a problem.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:48.100
Our lines are spread too thin, especially here at the center.

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:50.790
We need to dispatch reinforcements immediately.

00:21:52.030 --> 00:21:52.650
Do you agree?

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:59.520
Notify the Jem'Hadar. Order them to reinforce the center of their lines.

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:02.960
Now what?

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:07.410
Emergency power engaged.

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:13.820
Pounder. Relieved to see that you're alright.

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:15.900
Long range communications are down.

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:19.120
I can't contact the Jem'Hadar.

00:22:19.610 --> 00:22:21.000
Of course I'll keep trying.

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:22.860
What caused the power failure?

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:24.860
I'm afraid it was sabotage.

00:22:25.350 --> 00:22:29.430
Almost every Dominion installation on Cardassia Prime has suffered damage.

00:22:31.020 --> 00:22:31.440
Demar.

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:36.030
We captured some of the terrorists, but they're not soldiers.

00:22:36.110 --> 00:22:38.070
They're ordinary citizens.

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:44.700
Telling me that the Cardassian people are rising up against us?

00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:47.960
I'm sure it's only a small number of malcontents.

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:50.300
But we have no way of knowing that, do we?

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:53.060
Founder, may I make a suggestion?

00:22:53.820 --> 00:22:57.660
Yes, I am sure that Broca would be very happy to hear what you have to say.

00:22:58.330 --> 00:22:59.970
If the Cardassian people...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.040
are responsible for these acts of terrorism.

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:05.560
If Tamar and his fanatics have turned them against us,

00:23:06.510 --> 00:23:09.300
then it's the people who should be punished.

00:23:09.890 --> 00:23:11.650
Now, what do you say to that?

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:14.060
Severely punished!

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:15.140
Awkward.

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:17.000
Well, I'm glad we all agree.

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:18.140
See to it.

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:37.140
In 24 minutes.

00:23:37.804 --> 00:23:44.044
If the Dominion hasn't been able to restore power to the capital, then the entire planet must be in chaos.

00:23:44.184 --> 00:23:44.944
I hope so.

00:23:45.612 --> 00:23:48.612
I'm afraid I was only able to find two more light sticks.

00:23:48.612 --> 00:23:50.612
There's more about the house somewhere, but I just need to...

00:23:50.612 --> 00:23:53.112
Just stop dawdling and give them to me.

00:23:53.112 --> 00:23:55.612
Oh, well, I remember that tone of voice.

00:23:55.788 --> 00:23:59.588
Reminds me of the demanding and inconsiderate boy you used to be.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.480
I haven't changed much, have I?

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:03.520
This is to send a clear message to the Dominion.

00:24:04.350 --> 00:24:06.670
The Cardassian people will fight to regain their freedom.

00:24:06.910 --> 00:24:08.950
I hope they realize their fight is just beginning.

00:24:09.150 --> 00:24:11.490
We're gonna have to hit the enemy again and harder this time.

00:24:11.650 --> 00:24:12.750
Well, that won't be easy.

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:14.730
They will have tightened their security.

00:24:14.950 --> 00:24:17.050
Well, that doesn't matter. We can't lose our momentum.

00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:18.450
Commander is right.

00:24:19.760 --> 00:24:22.060
We cannot rest until Cardassia is free.

00:24:22.570 --> 00:24:26.740
And when it is, we'll have you to thank for it.

00:24:28.130 --> 00:24:29.850
Without you, the rebellion...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.180
would have died in its infancy.

00:24:32.090 --> 00:24:33.030
Ironic, isn't it?

00:24:33.170 --> 00:24:36.530
The savior of Cardassia, a former Bajoran terrorist?

00:24:36.770 --> 00:24:38.630
Well, don't canonize me just yet.

00:24:41.490 --> 00:24:42.750
It's been 26 and a half minutes.

00:24:43.490 --> 00:24:45.410
Let's see what the Dominion has to say for itself.

00:24:45.960 --> 00:24:47.540
Citizens of Cardassia,

00:24:48.180 --> 00:24:51.940
this latest wave of vandalism directed against your Dominion

00:24:51.940 --> 00:24:54.010
allies must stop.

00:24:54.600 --> 00:24:55.600
I wouldn't count on it.

00:24:55.600 --> 00:24:58.360
We know that these disgraceful acts of sabotage

00:24:58.360 --> 00:24:59.840
were carried out by a mere hand

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:06.800
of extremists, but these radicals must come to realize that their disobedience will not be

00:25:06.800 --> 00:25:14.280
tolerated, that you, the Cardassian people, will suffer the consequences of their cowardly actions.

00:25:15.700 --> 00:25:26.510
Which is why I must inform you, a few moments ago Dominion troops reduced Licarian City to ashes.

00:25:27.080 --> 00:25:28.760
There were no survivors.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:36.320
Two million men, women, and children, gone in a matter of moments.

00:25:37.640 --> 00:25:43.460
For each act of sabotage committed against the Dominion, another Cardassian city will be destroyed.

00:25:44.500 --> 00:25:46.840
I implore you not to let that happen.

00:25:47.120 --> 00:25:53.430
Let us return to the spirit of friendship and cooperation between our peoples,

00:25:53.470 --> 00:25:59.460
so that together we can destroy our common enemies, the Federation.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:03.640
The Klemans, the Romulans, and all the others that stand against us.

00:26:07.590 --> 00:26:10.430
I should have killed that four dead jackal when I had the chance.

00:26:10.650 --> 00:26:11.330
You want another one?

00:26:12.080 --> 00:26:13.560
We'll attack Dominion headquarters.

00:26:14.510 --> 00:26:16.330
Chop off a snake's head and the body will die.

00:26:16.850 --> 00:26:17.250
Exactly.

00:26:17.780 --> 00:26:20.860
Damar, for the past two years, you've practically lived in that building.

00:26:21.500 --> 00:26:23.780
If you're asking me if I know a way in, the answer is no.

00:26:24.730 --> 00:26:26.570
Not without valid security protocol.

00:26:27.310 --> 00:26:27.990
We'll use force.

00:26:28.440 --> 00:26:29.840
We're going to need some kind of explosive.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:31.320
I'll get right on it.

00:26:32.100 --> 00:26:33.580
You're proposing a suicide.

00:26:33.960 --> 00:26:36.840
If you have nothing positive to say, Mila.

00:26:37.610 --> 00:26:38.950
Fred, I'll prepare some food.

00:26:39.520 --> 00:26:41.520
Nobody should die on an empty stomach.

00:26:46.200 --> 00:26:49.360
Sir, Chancellor Martok would like to speak to you and Admiral Ross.

00:26:49.720 --> 00:26:50.260
Put them through.

00:26:51.190 --> 00:26:55.220
Gentlemen, a magnificent victory lies before us.

00:26:55.820 --> 00:26:57.900
I trust those are prophetic words, Chancellor.

00:26:58.300 --> 00:26:58.880
They are.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.360
I've not forgotten the promise I made to both of you.

00:27:03.010 --> 00:27:06.150
That the three of us would share a bottle of blood wine in Cardassia Prime.

00:27:06.410 --> 00:27:07.130
A bottle?

00:27:08.300 --> 00:27:11.820
I brought a barrel of 2309.

00:27:11.960 --> 00:27:13.500
There is no finer vintage.

00:27:14.740 --> 00:27:16.460
Then I'll meet you both on Cardassia.

00:27:17.400 --> 00:27:18.820
We'll see who gets there first.

00:27:21.450 --> 00:27:23.270
Chancellor makes victory sound easy.

00:27:23.610 --> 00:27:24.770
He knows it won't be.

00:27:25.840 --> 00:27:27.020
Sisko to all hands.

00:27:27.430 --> 00:27:28.830
Prepare to engage the enemy.

00:27:56.780 --> 00:27:59.620
Say one thing for the Breen, they know how to pilot their ships.

00:28:00.060 --> 00:28:00.900
So do you, Ensign.

00:28:01.100 --> 00:28:01.760
Stay with him.

00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:04.120
I'm trying, but he's slippery.

00:28:04.610 --> 00:28:06.920
Mr. Worf, unable to lock target.

00:28:11.690 --> 00:28:13.850
We have two Jemadar ships closing after us.

00:28:14.070 --> 00:28:16.010
They're in 136 Mark IV.

00:28:16.270 --> 00:28:17.790
Evasive action pattern Delta.

00:28:19.360 --> 00:28:20.160
Hang on.

00:28:30.640 --> 00:28:31.480
Well done, Ensign.

00:28:31.940 --> 00:28:33.420
I lost the brain ship we were after.

00:28:33.830 --> 00:28:34.930
I wouldn't worry about it.

00:28:35.290 --> 00:28:36.990
There are plenty more to choose from.

00:28:49.660 --> 00:28:51.260
Hardly touched your meal.

00:28:52.120 --> 00:28:53.440
No wonder you're not looking well.

00:28:53.760 --> 00:28:56.720
I'm not looking well because I live in a cellar.

00:28:57.220 --> 00:28:58.800
Well, so does Leggett de Marr.

00:28:58.840 --> 00:28:59.640
And what about him?

00:29:00.030 --> 00:29:02.130
Well, he's finished everything on his plate,

00:29:02.460 --> 00:29:06.540
which explains why he is such a fine, handsome figure of a man.

00:29:06.740 --> 00:29:08.220
Oh, I'm afraid I don't follow you.

00:29:08.360 --> 00:29:08.920
I do.

00:29:09.180 --> 00:29:11.020
Mila, I believe you're falling in love.

00:29:11.280 --> 00:29:12.860
Oh, I'm old enough to be his mother.

00:29:13.540 --> 00:29:16.080
But, nonsense.

00:29:17.710 --> 00:29:18.190
Politicians.

00:29:21.440 --> 00:29:21.880
Ding dong.

00:29:22.780 --> 00:29:23.460
Who could that be?

00:29:24.020 --> 00:29:25.320
Uh, I'll go see.

00:29:34.760 --> 00:29:38.110
What's taking us so long?

00:29:38.640 --> 00:29:39.440
I don't know.

00:30:02.330 --> 00:30:02.550
Uh-uh.

00:30:45.390 --> 00:30:46.590
I can't look away for a second.

00:30:47.110 --> 00:30:48.130
Just fix the shoulder.

00:30:50.020 --> 00:30:50.280
Careful!

00:30:50.620 --> 00:30:52.540
Sit still or you'll end up with one arm shorter than the other.

00:30:52.700 --> 00:30:56.320
Don't do anything to beat me at darts.

00:30:56.540 --> 00:30:58.700
I haven't lost a game to you in months.

00:30:59.100 --> 00:30:59.920
I'm gonna miss her game.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:03.650
What are you talking about? You're gonna be fine.

00:31:04.370 --> 00:31:06.610
I'm leaving DS9, Julian. I'm moving back to Earth.

00:31:08.400 --> 00:31:08.640
Why?

00:31:09.300 --> 00:31:13.490
I've been offered a position at the Starfleet Academy, Professor of Engineering.

00:31:14.630 --> 00:31:14.850
When?

00:31:16.400 --> 00:31:17.180
When the war's over.

00:31:19.440 --> 00:31:19.740
I see.

00:31:20.320 --> 00:31:24.480
Somebody has to teach you officers the difference between a warp matrix flux capacitor

00:31:25.090 --> 00:31:27.800
and a self-sealing stem bolt.

00:31:27.900 --> 00:31:28.280
Of course.

00:31:30.030 --> 00:31:30.170
Close.

00:31:31.480 --> 00:31:33.020
Captain, Admiral Ross for you.

00:31:33.220 --> 00:31:33.660
On screen.

00:31:35.410 --> 00:31:36.930
The Romulan flagship's been destroyed.

00:31:37.150 --> 00:31:38.310
Their entire line is collapsing.

00:31:38.960 --> 00:31:39.700
We'll try to help.

00:31:40.170 --> 00:31:40.570
With what?

00:31:41.400 --> 00:31:43.300
Ben, we're losing too many ships.

00:31:43.440 --> 00:31:45.520
We've got to find a way to turn the Dominion's left flank.

00:31:45.820 --> 00:31:49.020
It's too well protected, but the lines are spread pretty thin in the middle.

00:31:50.820 --> 00:31:51.640
You help the Romulans.

00:31:51.860 --> 00:31:52.920
Martok and I'll hit the center.

00:31:53.620 --> 00:31:54.200
On my way.

00:31:54.710 --> 00:31:57.670
Dax, have attack wings 64 and 65 follow us.

00:31:57.830 --> 00:31:58.150
Aye, sir.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:01.240
Taking so long?

00:32:01.420 --> 00:32:06.040
Our engineers have assured me that our long-range communications will be restored momentarily.

00:32:06.600 --> 00:32:08.640
But you have been saying that for hours.

00:32:09.070 --> 00:32:12.170
In the meantime, there's no way of contacting our ships.

00:32:12.350 --> 00:32:15.210
No way of knowing how the battle is progressing.

00:32:15.530 --> 00:32:19.210
Founder, our troops have captured the traitor Damar.

00:32:20.190 --> 00:32:22.600
Finally, some good news.

00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:23.580
And there's more.

00:32:24.340 --> 00:32:27.240
Colonel Kira and Garrick have been apprehended with him.

00:32:27.530 --> 00:32:28.490
Even better.

00:32:29.240 --> 00:32:29.880
Shall I have them?

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:52.090
brought here. What for? Have them execute it. Immediately. With pleasure. Understood.

00:32:52.680 --> 00:32:59.970
It will be done at once. On your feet! Why? We prefer our prisoners to be stabbed.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:00.860
when they die.

00:33:02.890 --> 00:33:06.270
Does anyone have any last words?

00:33:07.770 --> 00:33:09.830
You may kill us, but Cardassia will never...

00:33:09.830 --> 00:33:10.110
Enough!

00:33:10.620 --> 00:33:11.880
Final words are not permitted.

00:33:12.820 --> 00:33:13.600
How disappointing.

00:33:14.890 --> 00:33:15.450
Ready weapons!

00:33:16.910 --> 00:33:26.190
On my mark, that's for Licarian City.

00:33:31.530 --> 00:33:35.520
Legodomar, I pledge my life to free Cardassia from the Dominion.

00:33:36.240 --> 00:33:37.540
With men like you on our side.

00:33:39.550 --> 00:33:39.950
They fail.

00:33:58.650 --> 00:33:59.890
Jebedar, ship off the port bow!

00:34:00.220 --> 00:34:01.540
Shields are down to 60%.

00:34:01.540 --> 00:34:03.720
This is no good.

00:34:04.170 --> 00:34:05.270
I have to get into sick bay.

00:34:06.360 --> 00:34:07.460
I'm kind of busy right now.

00:34:07.540 --> 00:34:08.100
That's an order.

00:34:08.380 --> 00:34:09.020
Look, Julian.

00:34:09.160 --> 00:34:09.920
You heard him, Chief.

00:34:11.180 --> 00:34:11.560
Yes, sir.

00:34:13.380 --> 00:34:14.480
Another German art to port.

00:34:15.600 --> 00:34:17.260
Transferring auxiliary power to port shields.

00:34:18.390 --> 00:34:20.710
Dax, we need some support from those attack fighters.

00:34:21.050 --> 00:34:21.390
Aye, sir.

00:34:22.730 --> 00:34:24.390
Bring ship off the starboard aft.

00:34:25.510 --> 00:34:27.750
Our fighters are either destroyed or under attack themselves.

00:34:28.760 --> 00:34:29.860
Ensign, get us out of here.

00:34:31.310 --> 00:34:32.170
I'm trying, sir.

00:34:47.700 --> 00:34:51.530
Sir, the Cardassians, they're attacking the other Dominion ships.

00:35:02.170 --> 00:35:03.270
They've switched sides.

00:35:04.410 --> 00:35:04.870
Yes!

00:35:05.380 --> 00:35:06.580
The timing couldn't be better.

00:35:07.310 --> 00:35:09.430
Come about and head for the center of their lines.

00:35:09.690 --> 00:35:11.530
This is our chance to punch through.

00:35:12.330 --> 00:35:12.850
Aye, sir.

00:35:17.980 --> 00:35:18.380
Founder.

00:35:18.920 --> 00:35:21.800
Our long-range communications are back online.

00:35:22.290 --> 00:35:23.350
It's about time.

00:35:28.590 --> 00:35:28.910
Leave it.

00:35:30.920 --> 00:35:31.420
What now?

00:35:32.320 --> 00:35:35.020
The Cardassian fleet has turned against us.

00:35:39.710 --> 00:35:43.350
Our forces pull back and regroup at Cardassia Prime.

00:35:44.390 --> 00:35:45.750
But we'll be totally surrounded.

00:35:46.280 --> 00:35:48.220
There will be no more running.

00:35:49.170 --> 00:35:53.640
We should have rid ourselves of the Cardassians at the first sign of rebellion.

00:35:56.480 --> 00:35:59.830
If I could talk to the rebels, get them to change their mind.

00:36:00.090 --> 00:36:02.970
Perhaps you could reawaken their patriotic spirit.

00:36:03.170 --> 00:36:03.630
Exactly!

00:36:04.330 --> 00:36:09.230
On the other hand, they're just as likely to convince you to betray us.

00:36:09.930 --> 00:36:12.820
Me? Betray you? Never!

00:36:13.150 --> 00:36:15.930
That's right. We are not going to give you that opportunity.

00:36:18.060 --> 00:36:19.930
Wait! You're making a terrible mistake!

00:36:20.110 --> 00:36:21.130
I don't think so.

00:36:21.190 --> 00:36:22.890
But I've done everything you've asked!

00:36:23.160 --> 00:36:25.720
I tell you I'm loyal! I believe in the Dominion!

00:36:26.190 --> 00:36:26.870
All right!

00:36:28.510 --> 00:36:29.580
I won't miss him.

00:36:31.020 --> 00:36:33.400
I want the Cardassians exterminated.

00:36:33.990 --> 00:36:34.530
Which ones?

00:36:34.940 --> 00:36:37.100
All of them. The entire population.

00:36:38.340 --> 00:36:40.320
That will take some time.

00:36:41.310 --> 00:36:43.410
Then I suggest that you begin at once.

00:36:59.160 --> 00:36:59.460
Captain!

00:37:00.060 --> 00:37:02.480
The Dominion forces are retreating towards Cardassia Prime.

00:37:03.400 --> 00:37:06.780
Sir, Admiral Ross and Chancellor Murtaugh would like to talk to you.

00:37:07.060 --> 00:37:07.600
On screen.

00:37:08.710 --> 00:37:12.270
I never thought I'd say this, but thank God for the Cardassians.

00:37:12.830 --> 00:37:15.370
As I predicted, the day is ours.

00:37:15.890 --> 00:37:17.180
Not yet, it isn't.

00:37:17.510 --> 00:37:20.740
Ben, we've driven the Dominion back into Cardassia Prime.

00:37:20.960 --> 00:37:22.760
We can keep them bottled up there indefinitely.

00:37:23.260 --> 00:37:25.300
What if they use this time to rebuild their fleet?

00:37:25.800 --> 00:37:26.400
He's right.

00:37:26.700 --> 00:37:29.980
The Dominion has displayed an ability to build ships at an impossible...

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:36.670
impressive rate. We should continue the attack. At what cost? We've already lost a third of our

00:37:36.670 --> 00:37:43.980
fleet, and we must see to it that those soldiers did not die in vain. Admiral, with the Cardassians

00:37:43.980 --> 00:37:52.020
joining us, we have an opportunity to put an end to this war once and for all. All right,

00:37:52.100 --> 00:37:59.740
gentlemen, we press on. My friends, songs will be sung about this day.

00:38:01.530 --> 00:38:06.900
All right, people. You heard the orders. Let's finish what we started.

00:38:21.430 --> 00:38:25.890
Let me guess. We're here.

00:38:27.360 --> 00:38:29.060
We've reached the end of one journey.

00:38:30.250 --> 00:38:32.050
And stand ready to begin another.

00:38:38.390 --> 00:38:39.470
What's the matter, Ducat?

00:38:40.180 --> 00:38:41.060
You look disappointed.

00:38:42.840 --> 00:38:47.080
Well, this may sound naive, but I was expecting to see fire.

00:38:48.080 --> 00:38:50.460
They are called the fire caves.

00:38:51.670 --> 00:38:52.790
And with good reason.

00:39:02.430 --> 00:39:04.950
Lano Calabosha Lano Novala

00:39:05.520 --> 00:39:08.080
Parom Karana Mokado Bojah

00:39:08.200 --> 00:39:10.580
Kose Nusomakora Kajani

00:39:10.820 --> 00:39:14.250
Lano Calo Kosta Mojan

00:39:45.610 --> 00:39:49.410
According to this map, it's a long way from the cargo door to the briefing room.

00:39:49.590 --> 00:39:51.590
That could be a problem if we get trapped in the corridor.

00:39:53.550 --> 00:39:54.010
What the hell?

00:39:54.560 --> 00:39:55.460
It's Jem'Hadar.

00:39:55.560 --> 00:39:57.260
They're leveling the city, building by building.

00:39:57.440 --> 00:39:58.460
Alright, we have to go now.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:04.880
inside the complex we stop at nothing until we capture the changeling for

00:40:04.880 --> 00:40:14.780
Cardassia for Cardassia Eric well during the years of my exile I imagined what it

00:40:14.780 --> 00:40:18.760
would be like to come home I even thought of living in this house again

00:40:18.760 --> 00:40:26.190
with Mila now she's dead and this house is about to be reduced to a pile of rubble

00:40:27.880 --> 00:40:28.940
Cardassia is gone

00:40:31.550 --> 00:40:36.330
I have an even better reason, Commander.

00:40:37.520 --> 00:40:38.140
Revenge.

00:41:00.120 --> 00:41:04.940
I rid myself of the prophets and shed a lifetime of hypocrisy.

00:41:14.540 --> 00:41:16.580
I've never seen you look so radiant.

00:41:17.290 --> 00:41:20.830
I feel like a young woman waiting for my lover to sweep me away.

00:41:21.420 --> 00:41:24.420
Do you give yourself willingly to the parades?

00:41:25.730 --> 00:41:28.160
Then call to them.

00:41:30.890 --> 00:41:48.100
Dora Paran, Yeh Lim Chao O'Kol Stomo John, Sheh Tayel Terah Novala Derahm

00:41:55.360 --> 00:41:57.320
Cisco Tobachir, report.

00:41:58.180 --> 00:41:59.780
Three dead, eight wounded, four of them critically.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:02.840
Doctor, I need every able-bodied crewman at their post.

00:42:03.020 --> 00:42:05.300
I won't keep anybody here a second longer than I have to, sir.

00:42:08.310 --> 00:42:09.670
Pretty well for a first date.

00:42:10.110 --> 00:42:10.670
What do you think, Captain?

00:42:12.200 --> 00:42:13.640
I'd say she did fine, then, sir.

00:42:16.500 --> 00:42:16.900
Dwarf.

00:42:18.260 --> 00:42:18.580
Sir.

00:42:18.860 --> 00:42:23.400
Phaser banks are fully charged, but we are down to 45 quantum torpedoes.

00:42:23.820 --> 00:42:24.580
That'll have to do.

00:42:26.140 --> 00:42:27.300
Are you holding up, old man?

00:42:28.160 --> 00:42:29.550
All things considered.

00:42:30.320 --> 00:42:31.600
I think I'd rather be on Riza.

00:42:32.340 --> 00:42:35.380
Well, that makes two of us.

00:42:39.940 --> 00:42:41.100
Have you seen these reports, Captain?

00:42:42.140 --> 00:42:44.840
The Dominion has begun destroying Cardassian cities.

00:42:45.750 --> 00:42:46.870
Millions of people are dying.

00:42:47.910 --> 00:42:50.170
Captain, we're approaching the Dominion defense perimeter.

00:42:51.420 --> 00:42:56.200
Well, let's see what they have waiting for us.

00:42:57.090 --> 00:42:57.710
On screen.

00:43:27.260 --> 00:43:27.700
Just one?

00:43:28.120 --> 00:43:29.540
I'm afraid it's a rather large problem.

00:43:30.250 --> 00:43:31.950
The cargo door is made of neutronium.

00:43:33.810 --> 00:43:36.530
Then the explosives we brought aren't even going to make a tent.

00:43:36.690 --> 00:43:37.590
You see the problem.

00:43:38.160 --> 00:43:38.640
What do we do?

00:43:38.940 --> 00:43:41.020
I don't know.

00:43:42.000 --> 00:43:43.140
But I'm through hiding in basements.

00:43:46.990 --> 00:43:48.630
Failed to see what is so funny, Garrick.

00:43:50.640 --> 00:43:51.620
Isn't it obvious?

00:43:52.160 --> 00:43:55.060
Here we are, ready to storm the castle.

00:43:55.540 --> 00:43:59.980
Willing to sacrifice our lives in the noble effort to slay the...

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:06.250
It's a minion beast in its lair, and we can't even get inside the gates.

00:44:14.460 --> 00:44:17.560
Just have them send the shapeshifter out to us.

00:44:22.330 --> 00:44:27.540
As I said, we have a problem.

00:44:31.150 --> 00:44:35.190
But I've come to depend on having you here at my side.

00:44:36.350 --> 00:44:40.050
Your advice to the Dominion has proven invaluable.

00:44:41.560 --> 00:44:43.000
Very well.

00:44:43.490 --> 00:44:49.330
If you feel the situation on the front lines demands your presence, I will not stand in your way.

00:44:50.140 --> 00:44:54.660
Knowing that you'll be leading our troops into battle is very reassuring.

00:45:04.220 --> 00:45:06.080
I still can't help but wonder.

00:45:07.370 --> 00:45:08.170
Wonder what?

00:45:08.440 --> 00:45:09.620
What's under that helmet?

00:45:11.440 --> 00:45:12.840
Braver man than you.

00:45:14.770 --> 00:45:19.860
Though I do find the shrillness of his voice very tiresome.

00:45:22.490 --> 00:45:23.820
Found it. What's wrong?

00:45:25.200 --> 00:45:29.540
I'm dying. What's wrong?

00:45:30.830 --> 00:45:32.410
Perhaps you should rest for a while.

00:45:33.030 --> 00:45:34.550
Revert to your natural state.

00:45:35.360 --> 00:45:39.370
I haven't been able to change form in weeks.

00:45:42.570 --> 00:45:48.260
It's ironic, isn't it, that I should die as a solid?

00:45:48.640 --> 00:45:49.520
You're not going to die.

00:45:51.080 --> 00:45:54.320
You're a loyal way.

00:45:54.500 --> 00:45:58.950
The only solid I have ever trusted.

00:46:00.570 --> 00:46:03.090
I live only to serve you.

00:46:04.250 --> 00:46:05.710
And you have served me well.

00:46:08.700 --> 00:46:09.760
I don't mind dying.

00:46:11.500 --> 00:46:16.440
It's knowing that my entire race is dying of the same illness.

00:46:16.720 --> 00:46:19.770
And there is nothing I can do about it.

00:46:21.980 --> 00:46:25.120
I would give my life to save yours.

00:46:27.180 --> 00:46:29.280
If only it were that simple.

00:46:34.320 --> 00:46:36.020
What if I give myself up? Pretend to be a prisoner?

00:46:36.850 --> 00:46:37.690
Kill you on sight.

00:46:37.990 --> 00:46:39.290
And us, along with you.

00:46:41.310 --> 00:46:41.710
Kogodur.

00:46:43.110 --> 00:46:46.640
I didn't do anything wrong! I'm not a traitor! Please!

00:46:47.330 --> 00:46:48.590
Let me speak to the founder!

00:46:49.540 --> 00:46:50.700
No! No!

00:47:00.890 --> 00:47:01.130
Thank you.

00:47:31.820 --> 00:47:34.150
Remember his orders. We stop for nothing.

00:47:40.940 --> 00:47:42.880
We have a security breach.

00:47:43.620 --> 00:47:45.020
The guards will deal with it.

00:47:48.100 --> 00:47:49.000
Is there a problem?

00:47:49.630 --> 00:47:53.080
The guards. There's only a handful left in the building.

00:47:53.240 --> 00:47:56.100
I sent the rest to help eradicate the Cardassians.

00:47:59.020 --> 00:47:59.980
You two, get out.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:06.620
there and see that no one gets through that door you stay here in case they

00:48:06.620 --> 00:48:16.620
fail we'll launch a three-pronged attack the Romulans and our new

00:48:16.620 --> 00:48:20.570
Cardassian allies will engage the Jemadar forces the Klingons will target

00:48:20.570 --> 00:48:25.300
the Breen and the Federation will take on the orbital weapon platforms any

00:48:26.220 --> 00:48:29.320
questions when do we go as soon as everyone's in position

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.450
That would be a glorious battle.

00:48:32.830 --> 00:48:33.650
But a costly one.

00:48:34.400 --> 00:48:37.100
Estimates project our casualties to be as high as 40%.

00:48:37.990 --> 00:48:39.610
There's no telling how much higher they'll

00:48:39.610 --> 00:48:41.290
go once we send in our ground forces.

00:48:41.700 --> 00:48:43.560
The Dominion is beaten, and they know it.

00:48:44.760 --> 00:48:46.960
But they're going to make us pay for every kilometer

00:48:46.960 --> 00:48:47.680
of the planet.

00:48:48.470 --> 00:48:49.070
Yes, they will.

00:48:52.050 --> 00:48:52.950
Let's get on with it.

00:48:54.890 --> 00:48:55.630
Godspeed, everyone.

00:48:56.260 --> 00:48:59.970
Kepler found it.

00:49:00.410 --> 00:49:02.550
Perhaps we should consider finding a safer location.

00:49:03.140 --> 00:49:04.460
And just where would that be?

00:49:21.750 --> 00:49:25.690
Colonel Kira, what a pleasant surprise.

00:49:26.650 --> 00:49:27.590
Pleasures are mine.

00:49:28.080 --> 00:49:29.970
The Federation fleet is...

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:35.840
surrounded the planet. I want you to contact the Jem'Hadar and the Breen and you order their ships

00:49:35.840 --> 00:49:42.970
to stand down. And order the troops on Cardassia to do the same. I will do no such thing. Tell me,

00:49:43.690 --> 00:49:54.290
where's my old friend Tamar? Namar's dead. What a pity. He died trying to free Cardassia. What's left of it?

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:05.270
I wish you hadn't done that.

00:50:06.930 --> 00:50:08.890
That was Weyoun's last clone.

00:50:09.830 --> 00:50:11.190
I was hoping you'd say that.

00:50:14.390 --> 00:50:17.240
This war's over. You lost.

00:50:17.820 --> 00:50:18.280
Have I?

00:50:21.140 --> 00:50:26.130
I think you'll find that neither the Jem'Hadar or the Breen will agree with that assessment.

00:50:27.490 --> 00:50:29.410
They will fight to the last man.

00:50:30.160 --> 00:50:31.300
And what will that accomplish?

00:50:33.450 --> 00:50:34.330
Isn't it obvious?

00:50:36.410 --> 00:50:41.410
You may win this war, Commander, but I promise you, when it is over,

00:50:41.740 --> 00:50:46.110
you will have lost so many ships, so many lives,

00:50:46.990 --> 00:50:50.550
that your victory will taste as bitter as defeat.

00:51:01.120 --> 00:51:02.960
We're glad to find you in one piece, Commander.

00:51:03.330 --> 00:51:03.970
Very glad.

00:51:04.360 --> 00:51:05.060
What's your status?

00:51:06.440 --> 00:51:08.180
Only three of us made it to the briefing room.

00:51:08.600 --> 00:51:09.520
What about Damar?

00:51:10.620 --> 00:51:11.120
He's dead.

00:51:13.850 --> 00:51:14.990
Is your position secure?

00:51:15.390 --> 00:51:17.350
I don't think the Jem'Hadar will attack.

00:51:17.490 --> 00:51:21.650
They won't risk endangering the Founder, and she's in pretty bad shape.

00:51:21.870 --> 00:51:25.280
She just sits at her desk, deteriorating.

00:51:25.530 --> 00:51:29.970
If she dies before ordering the Jem'Hadar to surrender, then they will fight to the last.

00:51:31.400 --> 00:51:36.140
Captain, I should beam down there. The Founder will speak to me. I can reason with her.

00:51:37.660 --> 00:51:39.860
You haven't had much success with her in the past.

00:51:39.920 --> 00:51:42.710
It's worth a try. Think of the lives it could save.

00:51:45.440 --> 00:51:51.500
Very well. Commander, tell the Founder that Odo is going to pay her a visit.

00:52:04.120 --> 00:52:11.580
Tarnu porono olkes paran lunokala boshar lanu.

00:52:15.870 --> 00:52:16.370
After you.

00:52:19.020 --> 00:52:19.660
I'm honored.

00:52:29.350 --> 00:52:29.750
After you.

00:52:51.920 --> 00:52:53.780
Parés demand a sacrifice.

00:52:54.320 --> 00:52:56.200
Someone worthy of them.

00:52:56.760 --> 00:52:58.100
Who better than you?

00:53:18.810 --> 00:53:27.090
I offer you this life as nourishment, to feed your hunger, to fuel the fires that will set you free.

00:53:30.220 --> 00:53:34.430
I am Mojan, I am yours now and forever.

00:53:46.460 --> 00:53:46.840
Maurice.

00:53:47.040 --> 00:53:55.750
But yourself, I don't trust her.

00:53:56.960 --> 00:53:57.820
But you trust me.

00:54:01.630 --> 00:54:02.610
That's all I need to know.

00:54:06.080 --> 00:54:06.520
Constable.

00:54:06.910 --> 00:54:07.310
Garrick.

00:54:09.030 --> 00:54:10.330
You're looking well, Odo.

00:54:11.310 --> 00:54:12.450
Thank you for seeing me.

00:54:13.790 --> 00:54:15.230
It's always good to see you.

00:54:16.490 --> 00:54:19.870
But I have no intention of surrendering my forces.

00:54:21.070 --> 00:54:23.110
It would be a sign of weakness on my part.

00:54:23.830 --> 00:54:29.060
An invitation to the solids to cross into the Gamma Quadrant and destroy the Great Link.

00:54:29.370 --> 00:54:29.970
Believe me.

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:35.610
I'm well aware that the Federation has its flaws, but a desire for conquest isn't one of them.

00:54:35.770 --> 00:54:41.020
And what of the Klingons and the Romulans? Can you make that claim for them too?

00:54:41.970 --> 00:54:45.930
The Klingon and Romulan empires are in no shape to wage war against anyone.

00:54:46.700 --> 00:54:48.740
Besides, the Federation wouldn't allow it.

00:54:49.950 --> 00:54:53.750
The Dominion has spent the last two years trying to destroy the Federation.

00:54:54.150 --> 00:54:58.070
And now you're asking me to put our fate in their hands.

00:54:59.220 --> 00:54:59.480
Yes.

00:55:04.000 --> 00:55:06.020
I don't have your faith in the solitude.

00:55:06.780 --> 00:55:08.220
Perhaps I can change your mind.

00:55:10.780 --> 00:55:11.480
Link with me.

00:55:15.740 --> 00:55:17.900
I'm afraid I can't link with you, Odor.

00:55:18.280 --> 00:55:21.040
My disease prevents me from changing form.

00:55:21.750 --> 00:55:25.110
If we link, I believe I can cure you.

00:55:25.580 --> 00:55:27.780
That's a very bad idea, Constable.

00:55:27.880 --> 00:55:28.440
I agree.

00:55:29.040 --> 00:55:29.960
Narice, I know where you are.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:41.430
I'm doing. Please take my hand. And if you cure me, what will you ask in return? All I ask is that

00:55:41.430 --> 00:55:51.440
you link with me. I'm warning you, Odo. Maurice, can you make so?

00:56:20.960 --> 00:56:24.130
That won't be necessary, will it?

00:56:31.530 --> 00:56:35.130
If you will stand aside, I'll order the Jem'Hadar to cease fire.

00:56:37.480 --> 00:56:39.880
I suggest we secure her in a containment field.

00:56:40.220 --> 00:56:43.300
Don't worry, Garak. She won't try to escape.

00:56:44.260 --> 00:56:47.780
She's agreed to stand trial and accept responsibility for what she's done.

00:56:54.720 --> 00:56:57.460
I insist on going back to the Gamma Quadrant to cure her people.

00:56:58.340 --> 00:56:59.400
There's no need for that.

00:57:02.080 --> 00:57:03.280
I'm going in her place.

00:57:12.120 --> 00:57:14.390
Time I rejoined the Great Link.

00:57:28.530 --> 00:57:29.090
Yes!

00:57:30.570 --> 00:57:40.730
It's a moment worth savoring, to victory, hard fought, and well earned.

00:57:49.020 --> 00:57:49.380
What's wrong?

00:57:50.150 --> 00:57:51.210
Suddenly I'm not thirsty.

00:57:52.820 --> 00:57:53.380
Neither am I.

00:57:56.420 --> 00:57:58.700
Before you waste too many tears, remember.

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.760
These are Cardassians lying dead at your feet.

00:58:03.880 --> 00:58:07.500
Majorans would call this poetic justice.

00:58:08.460 --> 00:58:11.140
That doesn't mean I have to drink a toast over their bodies.

00:58:30.120 --> 00:58:39.760
A hundred million dead.

00:58:40.860 --> 00:58:43.100
Casualty reports still coming in.

00:58:46.720 --> 00:58:48.420
Well, aren't you going to congratulate me, Doctor?

00:58:48.980 --> 00:58:51.860
My exile is now officially over.

00:58:52.020 --> 00:58:56.100
I've returned home, or rather to what's left of it.

00:58:57.870 --> 00:58:59.970
Listen, I know that this must seem...

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:03.460
You know, some may say that we've gotten just what we deserved.

00:59:04.390 --> 00:59:06.850
After all, we're not entirely innocent, are we?

00:59:07.320 --> 00:59:10.100
And I'm not just speaking of the Bajoran occupation.

00:59:10.630 --> 00:59:14.060
No, our whole history is one of arrogant aggression.

00:59:15.670 --> 00:59:19.720
We've collaborated with the Dominion, betrayed the entire Alpha Quadrant.

00:59:20.610 --> 00:59:23.150
Oh, no, no, there's no doubt about it.

00:59:23.830 --> 00:59:26.030
We are guilty as charged.

00:59:28.340 --> 00:59:29.980
You and I both know that the Cardassians...

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:34.210
There are strong people. They'll survive. Cardassia will survive.

00:59:34.450 --> 00:59:39.930
Oh, please, Doctor. Spare me your insufferable Federation optimism.

00:59:40.330 --> 00:59:44.370
Of course it'll survive, but not as the Cardassia I knew.

00:59:46.100 --> 00:59:52.260
We had a rich ancient culture. Our literature, music, art was second to none.

00:59:56.240 --> 00:59:56.860
How much of it...

01:00:02.270 --> 01:00:08.570
Are many of our best people, our most gifted minds.

01:00:14.660 --> 01:00:23.420
Oh, it's quite a good friend.

01:00:24.840 --> 01:00:26.360
I'm going to miss our lunches together.

01:00:27.930 --> 01:00:29.090
Sure, we'll see each other again.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:39.140
I like to think so, but one can never say we live in uncertain times.

01:01:00.510 --> 01:01:07.980
The war between the Dominion and the Federation Alliance is now over.

01:01:11.600 --> 01:01:16.800
Four hundred years ago, a victorious general spoke the following words at the end of another costly war.

01:01:18.440 --> 01:01:21.810
Today the guns are silent. A great tragedy has ended.

01:01:23.020 --> 01:01:29.290
We have known the bitterness of defeat and the exaltation of triumph, and from both we have learned.

01:01:30.440 --> 01:01:31.520
There can be no going back.

01:01:33.440 --> 01:01:38.480
We must move forward to preserve in peace what we've won in war.

01:01:47.990 --> 01:01:49.720
It's up to you now, Odo.

01:01:57.760 --> 01:01:58.980
You're coming to VIX tonight, right?

01:01:59.180 --> 01:01:59.980
I will be there.

01:02:00.030 --> 01:02:02.010
But I will not dance.

01:02:02.740 --> 01:02:03.580
Who's asking?

01:02:04.350 --> 01:02:04.990
Commander War.

01:02:05.350 --> 01:02:06.950
Captain, can you spare a moment?

01:02:07.400 --> 01:02:07.740
Yes, sir.

01:02:08.700 --> 01:02:11.240
We've been discussing your plans for the future.

01:02:13.280 --> 01:02:15.080
I was not aware I had any plans.

01:02:15.680 --> 01:02:19.300
Commander, how would you feel about being named Federation Ambassador to Kronos?

01:02:20.830 --> 01:02:22.170
I am not a diplomat.

01:02:22.640 --> 01:02:24.360
And I am not a politician.

01:02:25.400 --> 01:02:28.960
But sometimes fate plays cruel tricks on us, War.

01:02:30.440 --> 01:02:32.520
Come, Kronos needs you.

01:02:33.020 --> 01:02:34.400
And what's more, I need you.

01:02:37.130 --> 01:02:38.490
You helped him become chancellor.

01:02:39.210 --> 01:02:40.710
He can't very well turn your back on him now.

01:02:44.050 --> 01:02:46.170
Well, my first loyalty is to you, Captain.

01:02:47.170 --> 01:02:48.090
Thank you, Mr. Warfowl.

01:02:49.080 --> 01:02:50.520
Probably regret this in the morning,

01:02:50.640 --> 01:02:53.780
but if it's what you want, then by all means.

01:02:58.390 --> 01:02:59.610
It has been a great honor.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:00.820
serving with you.

01:03:01.540 --> 01:03:02.540
The honor is mine.

01:03:05.600 --> 01:03:06.180
I accept.

01:03:07.080 --> 01:03:07.640
Excellent.

01:03:10.320 --> 01:03:13.380
An ambassador who'll go targ hunting with me.

01:03:14.940 --> 01:03:19.380
Well, perhaps being chancellor won't be so bad after all.

01:03:19.940 --> 01:03:21.020
Congratulations, Warp.

01:03:27.770 --> 01:03:28.230
You'll be going.

01:03:30.440 --> 01:03:30.740
Soon.

01:03:33.060 --> 01:03:36.650
You could come back, you know, once you've cured your people.

01:03:39.420 --> 01:03:39.640
Could.

01:03:42.250 --> 01:03:43.250
But you're not going to do that.

01:03:52.140 --> 01:03:54.450
Feelings for you will never change.

01:03:55.490 --> 01:03:58.630
But I have this.

01:04:00.320 --> 01:04:01.620
My people need me.

01:04:03.540 --> 01:04:05.300
They need to know what I know.

01:04:06.160 --> 01:04:11.900
To learn what I've learned from living among solids.

01:04:14.560 --> 01:04:16.640
It's the only way they'll ever learn to trust you.

01:04:16.800 --> 01:04:20.320
You don't have to justify your decision.

01:04:23.560 --> 01:04:24.260
It's just one thing.

01:04:28.010 --> 01:04:29.970
I'd like to take you back to your own.

01:04:30.190 --> 01:04:37.490
I didn't like that. I didn't like that very much.

01:04:40.610 --> 01:04:45.960
Hey, Bally, if you're here for another game of Go Fish, I'm a little busy right now.

01:04:46.360 --> 01:04:53.060
Actually, I'm here for the end of the war. Goodbye to Chief O'Brien, goodbye to Odo, goodbye to Wharf Party.

01:04:53.340 --> 01:04:54.040
At the bar.

01:04:56.470 --> 01:04:59.980
No, seriously, Miles, you know, I envy you. Going back to Earth, a chance to...

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:05.120
to enjoy paradise again any idea where you're gonna live no keiko and i are still mulling over

01:05:05.120 --> 01:05:10.560
a few possibilities have you ever considered minsk i don't think that's on our list new orleans is a

01:05:10.560 --> 01:05:18.510
gorgeous city i've heard great things about paris minsk jade zia loved rio oh you certainly got a

01:05:18.510 --> 01:05:24.190
lot of choices yeah too many who minsk well wherever you decide to go i'm sure that you

01:05:24.190 --> 01:05:29.460
and keiko will both be very happy listen julian i know earth isn't exactly around the corner but

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:37.320
expect you to visit. I intend to. Yeah, you and me, take a little trip to Texas. Standing side by side

01:05:37.320 --> 01:05:43.640
in front of the Alamo. The real Alamo. Gee, it's gonna be great. Absolutely. I don't see how great

01:05:43.640 --> 01:05:49.730
it will be. Earth's nothing more than a rotating ball of boredom. If you ask me, you'd be better

01:05:49.730 --> 01:05:55.030
off staying here. And that goes for... You and war as well. Don't tell me you're getting sentimental.

01:05:55.960 --> 01:05:58.330
Me? Not a chance.

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:01.240
I just don't like change.

01:06:01.870 --> 01:06:02.930
You better get used to it.

01:06:03.010 --> 01:06:04.990
Things are going to be pretty different around here now.

01:06:09.220 --> 01:06:11.840
To the best crew any captain ever had,

01:06:12.760 --> 01:06:14.720
this may be the last time we're all together.

01:06:16.380 --> 01:06:18.240
But no matter what the future holds,

01:06:19.400 --> 01:06:22.330
no matter how far we travel, a part of us,

01:06:23.550 --> 01:06:27.000
a very important part, will always remain here

01:06:27.000 --> 01:06:29.560
on Deep Space Nine.

01:06:36.680 --> 01:06:41.530
Ladies and gentlemen, tonight is a very special night for some friends of mine.

01:06:42.690 --> 01:06:44.110
They've been together a long time.

01:06:45.000 --> 01:06:49.180
Look like the man said, last forever.

01:06:50.580 --> 01:06:55.560
So, gang, someday.

01:07:10.140 --> 01:07:13.760
Just thinking of

01:07:34.280 --> 01:07:56.050
With your smile so warm and your cheeks so soft, there is nothing for me but to look just the way through.

01:08:04.660 --> 01:08:19.290
Which will tend to part

01:08:34.860 --> 01:08:45.500
Touching my dog

01:09:00.160 --> 01:09:04.890
I will feel the glow just thinking of...

01:09:34.320 --> 01:09:36.940
Dorotooka Brithi Paran!

01:09:38.210 --> 01:09:39.830
Ostamburgian, come to me!

01:09:41.940 --> 01:09:42.500
Thank you!

01:10:07.090 --> 01:10:07.750
Ah

01:10:33.000 --> 01:10:38.370
I understand now, but I have to do what I was meant to do.

01:10:39.580 --> 01:10:45.270
Pasadena Bajor to the fire caves.

01:10:45.430 --> 01:10:46.090
I'll go with you.

01:10:46.350 --> 01:10:49.920
No, I have to do this alone.

01:11:05.050 --> 01:11:10.920
Did you really think the Pah Wraiths would choose you as their emissary?

01:11:12.630 --> 01:11:26.100
Soon the Pah Wraiths will burn across Bajor, the Celestial Temple, the Alpha Quadrant.

01:11:26.780 --> 01:11:27.920
Can you picture it?

01:11:28.580 --> 01:11:29.900
An entire universe!

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:45.040
set in flames to burn for all eternity prophets have sent me a gift their

01:11:47.840 --> 01:11:55.540
beloved emissary sent forth like an avenging angel to slay the demon I

01:11:55.880 --> 01:11:58.950
should have known the demon would be you go on

01:12:00.320 --> 01:12:01.700
Kill me if you can.

01:12:08.320 --> 01:12:10.380
You have to do better than that, Captain.

01:12:16.700 --> 01:12:17.880
This is too easy.

01:12:20.500 --> 01:12:21.380
That's it.

01:12:21.540 --> 01:12:22.600
Come closer.

01:12:22.920 --> 01:12:23.740
That's it.

01:12:32.620 --> 01:12:51.960
now bow to me i said bow you dick then why are you the one on your knees first verminion

01:12:51.960 --> 01:12:59.640
now the parade you have a talent for picking the losing sides benjamin please we've known each

01:12:59.640 --> 01:12:59.920
to

01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:06.260
long. And since this is the last time we will ever be together, let's try to speak

01:13:06.260 --> 01:13:13.480
honestly. We've both had our victories and our defeats. Now it's time to resolve

01:13:13.480 --> 01:13:19.080
our differences and face the ultimate truth. I've warned Benjamin.

01:13:24.310 --> 01:13:29.960
Padreth will never conquer anything. Not Basil, not the celestial...

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:44.190
temple and certainly not the alpha quadrant and who's going to stop us i am you can't even stand

