01:16:50.480 --> 01:16:51.140
Let's go home.

01:17:01.950 --> 01:17:02.610
Oh, God.

01:17:07.220 --> 01:17:14.200
Sid, our prophets warned us.

01:17:20.740 --> 01:17:21.780
It's difficult to explain.

01:17:24.460 --> 01:17:25.280
It's not linear.

01:17:26.450 --> 01:17:26.750
It is.

01:17:30.570 --> 01:17:42.840
destiny. Prophets saved me, Cassidy. I'm their emissary, and they still have a great deal for

01:17:42.840 --> 01:17:55.830
me to do. There's much to learn. Be back.

01:18:00.760 --> 01:18:01.540
Maybe a year.

01:18:01.740 --> 01:18:13.900
I'll be waiting.

01:18:19.910 --> 01:18:21.570
Cass, can you hear me?

01:18:25.990 --> 01:18:27.950
You seem pretty far away for a second.

01:18:30.830 --> 01:18:31.490
I was talking.

01:20:00.890 --> 01:20:01.050
Thank you.

01:21:30.220 --> 01:21:30.420
Bye.

01:22:24.800 --> 01:22:26.810
Sure, I've never been good at goodbyes.

01:22:26.910 --> 01:22:29.440
I feel a lot of people that are disappointed.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:33.760
If they don't know how I feel about them now, a few parting words won't make the difference.

01:22:34.060 --> 01:22:35.720
Aha! I knew it.

01:22:36.190 --> 01:22:38.830
When I saw the two of you slip out, I said to myself,

01:22:39.170 --> 01:22:46.480
that no good misanthropic, cantankerous changeling is trying to sneak off the station without anyone noticing.

01:22:46.820 --> 01:22:48.080
That was the idea.

01:22:48.660 --> 01:22:49.880
Well, it's not going to happen, is it?

01:22:50.360 --> 01:22:51.240
Apparently not.

01:22:52.870 --> 01:22:55.940
So, now that I'm here...

01:23:00.190 --> 01:23:01.750
Is there something you want to say to me?

01:23:02.640 --> 01:23:03.480
Such as?

01:23:04.080 --> 01:23:05.200
Such as?

01:23:06.700 --> 01:23:07.140
Goodbye.

01:23:08.170 --> 01:23:10.070
You certainly were a worthy adversary.

01:23:11.360 --> 01:23:14.940
Or maybe something with the words mutual respect in it.

01:23:16.000 --> 01:23:16.380
No.

01:23:17.460 --> 01:23:17.640
No.

01:23:18.150 --> 01:23:18.890
What do you mean no?

01:23:19.380 --> 01:23:20.180
I mean no.

01:23:21.030 --> 01:23:23.490
I have nothing I want to say to you.

01:23:23.750 --> 01:23:28.590
You're telling me that after all these years, after all we've been through, you're not even going to say goodbye to me?

01:23:29.320 --> 01:23:29.920
That's right.

01:23:32.940 --> 01:23:34.870
Norris, I'll be on the runabout.

01:23:35.090 --> 01:23:44.330
You get hard, Quentin.

01:23:44.330 --> 01:23:47.050
Car? What are you talking about?

01:23:47.210 --> 01:23:48.770
That man loves me.

01:23:49.860 --> 01:23:50.400
Couldn't you see?

01:23:51.380 --> 01:23:53.020
It was written all over his back.

01:24:35.880 --> 01:24:38.330
So different.

01:24:41.030 --> 01:24:41.430
Dying.

01:24:43.400 --> 01:24:43.860
Go to them.

01:24:52.690 --> 01:24:55.310
Please, tell everyone I'll miss them.

01:24:56.420 --> 01:24:57.020
Even Quark.

01:24:58.180 --> 01:24:59.080
Even Quark.

01:25:01.850 --> 01:25:02.890
But most of all...

01:25:38.760 --> 01:25:48.390
You always said I looked good in a tuxedo. This is the way I want you to remember me

01:26:48.370 --> 01:26:54.710
Nice work. Congratulations on your promotion, Lieutenant.

01:26:55.160 --> 01:26:59.400
Thank you, sir. I guess putting me in for a promotion was...

01:27:00.090 --> 01:27:02.110
One of Captain Sisko's last official acts.

01:27:02.620 --> 01:27:04.200
I'm sure he's very proud of you, Nock.

01:27:05.980 --> 01:27:06.960
I'd like to think so, sir.

01:27:07.840 --> 01:27:09.280
Now about the cargo inventories.

01:27:11.220 --> 01:27:12.020
I'll get right on it.

01:27:40.360 --> 01:27:42.860
It's really just part of the normal cardiac renewal process.

